        "title": "docs: add ClawHub glossary labels",
        "body": "## What Problem This Solves\n\nAdds missing zh-CN glossary entries for existing ClawHub documentation titles so generated localized docs can keep those labels stable.\n\nAI-assisted: yes.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe branch preserves the existing ClawHub mirrored navigation contract and only adds glossary labels for the existing `ClawHub CLI` and `Publishing on ClawHub` titles. It does not add local OpenClaw-owned ClawHub pages or remove any mirror-owned ClawHub routes.\n\n## User Impact\n\nReaders of localized docs get consistent ClawHub labels while the published ClawHub docs navigation continues to expose the routes supplied by the ClawHub mirror.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Branch rebased onto `origin/main` `6dfa4c27a3ad6e8cb60b6263c4aa665a93654a1d`; pushed head is `967a467484d9531a6d5b7275ad47e97ae4f950b8`.\n- Final diff against `origin/main`: `docs/.i18n/glossary.zh-CN.json` only, 8 insertions.\n- `git diff --check origin/main` - passed.\n- `pnpm docs:check-i18n-glossary` - passed.\n- `pnpm docs:map:check` - passed.",
